File Index

/MainContainer.tsx
Purpose: Top-level layout orchestrator — mounts MainMenuBar/FocusBarVitals plus every modal (Connect/Library/Account/Equipment/Plugins/Contribute/ScriptingHelp), owns the per-connection plugin host lifecycle (create on connect, diff-sync installed, shutdown on disconnect), and wires `useAutoLeveling(connectionId, isConnected)` through to `AutoLevelingWizard`. The active HUD shell is NOT chosen by a direct ternary — every render calls `resolveActiveTheme(hudThemeId, viewportWidth)` (features/hudLayout/themeRegistry.ts) and renders whichever `React.lazy` ShellComponent it resolves to inside a single `<Suspense>`, so adding a theme never touches this file. `hudThemeId` is live state (not read-once) kept in sync via a `ListenEvent` subscription to hudThemeStore's `HUD_THEME_CHANGED_EVENT`, so a Settings-UI theme change re-renders this component in place — it never unmounts/remounts, so the connection/plugin-host effects below are untouched by a theme switch. That resolved theme's styles are applied in a `useEffect` keyed on `activeTheme.id`; a SEPARATE effect, deliberately declared AFTER the plugin-registration effect (`pluginHost.enable()` on an unregistered id is a silent no-op), calls `activeTheme.onActivate?.()` so a theme can auto-enable a core plugin it depends on. `<Terminal/>` is rendered exactly once here via `createPortal(<Terminal/>, terminalHost)`, where `terminalHost` is a detached DOM node created ONCE (lazy `useState` initializer) and never swapped as the portal's container — a separate effect imperatively `.appendChild()`s that same node into whichever shell's `terminalSlotRef` div is currently attached. This indirection matters: passing a DIFFERENT container to `createPortal` on a later render (e.g. portaling straight into the current shell's own slot div) makes React unmount/remount the portaled subtree, which is exactly the xterm.js scrollback loss this hoist exists to prevent — confirmed as a real regression via live Playwright before landing this two-node version. `terminalHost` is also given `display: flex; min-height: 0; min-width: 0` (not just `width/height: 100%`) — every shell's own terminal slot (`.terminalBody`, `.playAreaTerminalShell`) is `display: flex` so that `Terminal.tsx`'s own `flex: 1` root divs can size themselves against it; without that on `terminalHost` too, Terminal's flex rules go inert one level deeper and its rendered height collapses to content-size while the slot's black background still fills the full flex-allocated space around it — a real gap, caught live by the user in compact mode (2026-09-20). 2026-09-13 (live-playtest fix): removed the `localStorage['autoleveling.wizard']` opt-out flag and its `AutoLevelingWizard`/`AutoLevelingModal` ternary — the wizard is now unconditionally the only auto-leveling UI rendered here, no fallback path exists to silently land a stale-flag browser back on the old modal (see AutoLevelingModal.tsx's entry in components/.annotated).
